## Claim under pressure

SPRINT **CAP-G2** (granular **fs** enforce):

| Slice | Path-A expectation |
|-------|--------------------|
| FsReadCap | `read_file` / `fs_read` / `path_exists` / `file_size` only; **no** write |
| FsWriteCap | `write_file` / `fs_write` only; **no** read / path_exists / file_size |
| FsCap | Legacy supersede for soft-granular preferred ops (one-wave compat) |
| Runtime | `oo_cap_require_fsread` / `oo_cap_require_fswrite` accept exact granular **or** `g_tok_fs`; wrong granular exit fail-closed |
| Overlay | Keep `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR` fail-closed write allowlist (T3 **6.4**); do not weaken |
| Symlink | Leaf / parent symlink escape under writedir → deny (realpath + `openat` `O_NOFOLLOW`) |
| Hardlink | **T3 residual honesty** — not claimed sealed (see residual ledger) |

Adversarial stance: treat **any** FsReadCap→write_file check OK or runtime write with `g_tok_fsread` as **CRIT fail-open** until dual-proved deny.

